 "overview": "The Medford Historical Commission and Medford Historic District Commission are civic bodies responsible for reviewing demolition applications, designating historically significant structures, managing local historic districts, and advancing preservation and archaeological initiatives across Medford. Meeting records held by the archive run from February 2024 through October 2026. Across this period, the commissions evaluated numerous residential and commercial demolition requests, monitored historic sites such as the Brooks Estate and Thomas Brooks Park, oversaw headstone and archaeological recovery work at municipal cemeteries, and advised on city zoning updates. As of October 2026, work continues on demolition delay public hearings, ground-penetrating radar and headstone restoration at Cross Street Cemetery, neighborhood survey reviews, and filling vacancies on the boards.",
