  {
   "name": "Demolition review and delay determinations",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The Historical Commission regularly assesses demolition applications through multi-stage reviews involving application acceptance, historical significance determinations, and preferably preserved hearings. Initial sessions evaluated properties such as 314 Winthrop Street, 27 Almont Street, and 38 Pearl Street, imposing delays or negotiating mitigated designs before lifting delays. The commission continued this process for numerous residential and civic structures across the city, including 110 Brooks Street, 56 Wareham Street, 4 Grove Street, and 47 Holton Street. Recent proceedings evaluated properties including 15 Maple Park Avenue (the Hegner Center) and multiple parcels on Mystic Avenue, finding properties not preferably preserved or scheduling future hearings into late 2026.",
