   "name": "Cross Street Cemetery assessment and archaeological restoration",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The commission oversaw extensive assessment, excavation, and restoration initiatives for the historic Cross Street Cemetery and its relocated headstones at Oak Grove Cemetery. Early actions included funding preliminary foundation fieldwork and managing state archaeological permitting for exploratory trenching. In January 2025, trenching uncovered historical artifacts and human remains, prompting expanded multi-year state coordination, headstone repair budgets, and pilot restorations for veteran markers. Restoration work continued through 2026, encompassing gravestone cleaning, discoveries of buried markers, and procurement for ground-penetrating radar testing.",
