  {
   "name": "Zoning reform and preservation ordinance initiatives",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "Commissioners engaged in ongoing reviews of local zoning proposals and potential preservation ordinances to safeguard historic architecture. The commission studied outside models, such as Reading's preservation zoning, and analyzed the impact of proposed up-zoning on character-defining pre-1900 buildings in East Medford along the Salem Street corridor. In 2026, the commission reviewed historic preservation incentives and dimensional waivers incorporated into the newly approved Medford Square zoning. Subsequent work examined Boston Avenue North and South zoning drafts, providing feedback to protect residential side streets before submitting recommendations to the City Council.",
