  {
   "name": "Local historic districts and Historic District Commission operations",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The bodies coordinated the establishment, regulation, and public outreach for local historic districts across Medford. Early actions included supporting the creation of the South Street Local Historic District, finalizing registry filings, and planning district signage. The Historic District Commission handled exterior certificates of appropriateness for properties on Hillside Avenue and Touro Avenue while exploring protections for other historic resources such as 44 Bradley Road and 41 Mystic Avenue. The commission also conducted community outreach, monitored proposed state legislation affecting historic districts, held educational sessions on insurance and materials, and pursued board recruitment.",
